+Generation is inverse: sample equally distributed quadratic point-layers,
+choose one layer uniformly, join that layer as a cycle, and attach every other
+point by tree edges.  The stored cycle is known before distracting edges are
+assembled.  Connectedness plus |E|=|V| proves the graph has exactly one cycle.
 
+The degree outlier attack is defeated because cycle vertices and most internal
+tree vertices all have degree three.  Greedy and random self-avoiding walks are
+drawn into balanced branches.  The obvious affine-tag ansatz fails because all
+layers have nonzero quadratic coefficient.  The successful domain reference
+algorithm is reported separately, as Track B requires: peel degree-one vertices
