+The paper's native K-Cycle problem asks for a simple cycle through every
+specified terminal of an undirected graph.  This module inverse-generates a
+connected unicyclic graph and retains its unique cycle as the witness.  Vertex
+names are points over a prime field.  Every point belongs to one of many
+quadratic curves sampled in exactly the same way; one uniformly chosen curve
+is used for the cycle, and the other points are mixed through attached trees.
 
-Wahlstrom's Definition 1 asks for a simple cycle through every terminal.  This
-module uses the native special case K=V, which Section 1 identifies with
-Hamiltonian Cycle.  The certificate is generated without solving the emitted
-graph: closed walks in a hidden even-degree root graph are composed first, and
-their root edges become vertices of its line graph.  Consecutive root edges in
-the composed Euler circuit are adjacent in the line graph, so the carried list
-is a Hamiltonian cycle by construction.
+The family is Track B.  A linear-time 2-core computation always recovers the
+cycle.  At the shipping size that mechanical scan is far too long to carry out
+in the no-tool evaluation context, while the terminal points determine the
+cycle's quadratic invariant in a compact amount of exact arithmetic.
