Find a K-cycle in the following finite undirected graph.

Definitions.
A vertex is named by an ordered pair [x,y] over GF(p), so both coordinates are integers in 0..p-1 and all arithmetic on coordinates is modulo p.
An undirected edge [x1,y1] -- [x2,y2] may be traversed in either direction.
A simple cycle is a cyclic sequence of distinct vertices in which every consecutive pair is an edge, including the last vertex followed by the first.
A K-cycle is a simple cycle containing every terminal in K; it may contain nonterminals.

