A workspace race just surfaced: while the hardening process held my line-graph module in memory, another active builder rewrote the same module into a different 1,600-vertex quadratic/unicyclic family and created its own scratch runs. I’m pausing edits and checking that process’s state and artifacts so I don’t overwrite concurrent work; the bare transcript I just obtained belongs to the in-memory line-graph version, not the module currently on disk, so it cannot be shipped against this file.
