codex
The competing hardening run was defeated at every completed level through 3,200 vertices and then its child process exited without a verdict—likely an external resource interruption rather than hardness. The concurrent builder itself is still active and has not modified the module since, so I’m continuing to wait rather than clobber its recovery/cleanup step.
codex
The first quadratic-tag construction failed hardness: every bare oracle solved it through repeated escalations, so I stopped that run rather than misreporting it. I’m restoring the stronger construction already evidenced in this workspace: it composes an Euler circuit in a hidden even-degree root graph and carries it through the line-graph transformation; the bare harness held at medium.
