Rejected after full construction and audit: the candidate clears generation and verification but fails hardness on both tracks.

- Track A fails because every generated line graph has a polynomial-time solution.
- Track B fails because Lehot’s optimal \(E+O(N)\) root-reconstruction algorithm plus Hierholzer costs about 328 graph-item visits, versus 224 operations for the intended shortcut. There is no meaningful compression gap. [Lehot’s result](https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.1145/321850.321853) confirms the linear algorithm.
- The paper’s exact K-cycle definition and \(O^*(2^{|K|})\) algorithm were verified from [arXiv:1301.1517](https://arxiv.org/pdf/1301.1517).

